ption":"Collagen","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3717-7b37-90d9-c174e192eb6c","description":"Cadmium","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3717-7987-8293-6405fc931336","description":"Calcitonin","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-3717-700e-babb-ffb3cf915932","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which lizard is able to change the color of its skin?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Chameleons often change color to signal mood or regulate body temperature, not just to blend into their surroundings.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-3717-7acb-b2ea-87c866ce0fd3","description":"Chameleon","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-3717-74e6-8e35-4c660636d352","description":"Slowworm","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3717-7f6f-8253-43bce6048543","description":"Iguana","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3717-7ad6-85ab-a5d2819816bd","description":"Turkish gecko","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-3717-77cb-ba3f-ef3ffddd3dc3","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the name for a small earthquake or tremor that occurs following a major one?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Aftershocks result from the Earth\'s crust adjusting to stress changes caused by a major earthquake, and they can continue for days or longer.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-3717-7e7d-be8a-4e0ec0a25af2","description":"An aftershock","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-3717-76c0-8051-9c274f0426f9","description":"A precursor","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3717-760f-8fd9-8c12296045da","description":"A temblor","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3717-7867-9365-e7f738771c86","description":"A seismic wave","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-3717-7318-842b-952e15a479b2","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is a ridge of sand that is piled up by the wind?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"A dune can migrate as wind carries sand g