ole-number increase represents a tenfold increase in measured wave amplitude.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-3718-76ae-a401-0ac6b072e8e0","description":"Richter","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-3718-7d73-88d6-181729b43d64","description":"Beaufort","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3718-7c45-bc1e-4000d9920bc5","description":"Schweizer","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3718-7251-90b8-2b0ce44df94e","description":"Hammer","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-3718-73f4-a218-96309fadeaf6","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which organism eats only meat?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Carnivores get their food from animals; herbivores eat plants, while omnivores eat both.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-3718-73c7-a2a6-f5d84107043a","description":"Carnivore","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-3718-775c-a599-99dfdca91252","description":"Herbivore","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3718-7f56-b06d-61ce3156c9fc","description":"Omnivore","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3718-7063-a45f-701d334c0b64","description":"Vegan","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-3718-76b7-9345-753821251d6d","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What animal is known as Orcinus orca?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Killer whale is the common name for Orcinus orca. Despite the name, it is the largest dolphin species.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-3718-7954-91fe-d7b0772ba9f0","description":"Killer whale","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-3718-7dba-b57e-57c74bf97d76","description":"Badger","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3718-72d2-b599-c348b969472b","description":"Orchard bee","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3718-734c-a72b-7b61ec8cc1fc","description":"Camel","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-3718-7200-a822-b4fc2cdf6a91","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which bird often stands on one leg?","difficul