_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3718-7028-b7c0-5ee4f0841e8b","description":"Hypothermia","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-3718-777c-b202-3dde86ceb900","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What paper size measures 210 mm \u00d7 297 mm?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"A4 belongs to ISO 216\'s A series, whose sheets keep the same proportions when each size is halved.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-3718-74d3-b469-399da8ff8f41","description":"A4","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-3718-7840-92bd-6dab33c619da","description":"A3","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3718-73c7-b348-74daa52d667b","description":"A5","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3718-7322-b907-d088593c719a","description":"A2","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-3718-73d4-b687-2895dd10b79c","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What do we call the center of an atom?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"The nucleus contains nearly all an atom\u2019s mass, with protons and neutrons held together by the strong nuclear force.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-3718-734e-8459-98eae0235ad4","description":"Nucleus","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-3718-78af-8dbe-c2833b0dada8","description":"Pivot","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3718-7ff6-a1f3-2b31a5794d60","description":"Epicenter","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3718-7208-b74a-a9a72aef214e","description":"Fulcrum","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-3718-7e3a-a164-d45ac5f26f94","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is futurology the study of?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Futurology uses trends across fields such as technology, economics, and society to explore possible scenarios; it does not claim certainty about The Future.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-3718-7d82-b0d5-3d843bffa038","description":"The Future","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-3718-7c26-9f47-cad6bd6dbf23","desc