ct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3718-77a7-a0bc-47eec28b3edd","description":"1 Month","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-3718-70d9-90dd-933a5b61c752","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the name of a shape with three sides?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"A triangle\u2019s interior angles add up to 180 degrees in Euclidean geometry, and its three sides make it the simplest polygon.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-3718-7967-9c82-719e13524d79","description":"Triangle","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-3718-7f2f-91c6-2fb4dd46c301","description":"Square","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3718-7561-95bd-48013d0fac11","description":"Parallelogram","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3718-7913-8195-a96575151d70","description":"Trapezoid","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-3718-77e8-97f5-5c11f1f292f2","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What gas is produced during the incomplete combustion of charcoal?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Carbon monoxide forms when carbon-containing fuel burns with insufficient oxygen. It is dangerous because it binds to hemoglobin and reduces the blood\u2019s ability to carry oxygen.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-3718-7024-a581-69a082ef4ffe","description":"Carbon monoxide","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-3718-7d54-9158-fab05fe28729","description":"Carbon dioxide","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3718-7113-8192-9c7ee6ca5738","description":"Methane","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3718-7654-9282-aa1094a5b26c","description":"Nitrogen","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-3718-777d-9e9a-f6410999ccde","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"In which part of the human throat is the epiglottis located?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"The larynx houses the epiglottis, a flap of cartilage that helps keep food and liquid out of the airway during swallowing.","alterna