,"difficulty":1,"explanation":"Isaac Newton also built an early practical reflecting telescope, which used mirrors rather than lenses to form an image.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-3719-788c-a53e-09859ee74d18","description":"Isaac","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-3719-71d3-9325-a0b86a06a1f0","description":"Albert","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3719-746d-93e6-6cc37a59ae6c","description":"Herbert","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3719-7cf3-8b49-2e6a83f36a4a","description":"Luigi","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-3719-7ff8-aec0-fb5a50090dde","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the name of the red gem that symbolizes health and wisdom, and is the birthstone for July?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Rubies and sapphires are both forms of corundum; trace amounts of chromium give rubies their red color.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-3719-7c3a-b8ae-5033dd44b795","description":"Ruby","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-3719-742a-a196-8722d85d97bf","description":"Emerald","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3719-7ea5-ab2b-2302eee2c439","description":"Sapphire","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3719-7278-b3a0-296f94667e9f","description":"Diamond","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-3719-7ec5-ac85-7a798bf1691a","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the name of the salty, watery fluid secreted by sweat glands?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Perspiration is produced mainly by eccrine glands, and its evaporation helps cool the body.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-3719-7390-9032-8d6c43027c49","description":"Perspiration","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-3719-7e2f-a307-08dfc509ccc0","description":"Saline","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3719-7e83-a54d-8623402cab43","description":"Lactate","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3719-7747-b90b-fe0fd51fbe6e","description":"Water","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"0