9ce2f2","description":"Speed","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3719-7c48-988e-4e87179f6f60","description":"Force","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-3719-76cd-b1b9-2d096645a461","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which of these diseases is characterized by skin lesions?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Leprosy is caused by bacteria and can affect both the skin and peripheral nerves, sometimes causing numbness or weakness.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-3719-7ba2-8c10-7fb4b00d8c51","description":"Leprosy","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-3719-7925-85d4-289f633cbe2d","description":"Pneumonia","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3719-7bf9-bfea-73bdfcae580a","description":"Cholera","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3719-7e22-9154-f81d236b8f09","description":"Influenza","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-3719-75dd-b161-d777186c9b35","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which fish has whisker-like feelers next to its mouth?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Catfish use their barbels, which contain sensory receptors, to locate food, especially when visibility is poor.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-3719-74b7-80a3-18e8de4ff02c","description":"Catfish","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-3719-702b-98f4-542cec37a7ac","description":"Dogfish","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3719-7b90-bd5b-cc22904ce205","description":"Lungfish","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3719-7d06-81ae-e00b2de24e05","description":"White shark","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-3719-7287-a81c-b81c4bbe88e6","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What does LCD stand for?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Liquid Crystal Display screens modulate light rather than producing it at each pixel, so many use a separate backlight.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-3719-742d-9a03-e3aa78818bfb","description":"Liquid Crystal Display","corre